OL,3,GNEWSAStrangers at festival help
OL,4,Aautistic man realise dream
OL,5,
OL,6,FStrangers at a music event helped an
OL,7,Fautistic man "realise all of his
OL,8,Fdreams" after he attended his
OL,9,Ffirst-ever festival alone.
OL,11,FAdam James, 23, from High Wycombe in
OL,12,FBuckinghamshire, said his father, Andy,
OL,13,Fwas very concerned for his safety
OL,14,Fbefore he travelled to Boomtown
OL,15,FFestival in Hampshire.
OL,17,FBut Andy's fears "melted away" after
OL,18,FAdam befriended a group of
OL,19,Ffestival-goers who invited him to camp
OL,20,Fwith them and helped ensure he enjoyed
OL,21,Fthe five-day event.
OL,23,APub: 24-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,343,340,200,160,0,100
